<ServiceLayout title="Whiplash" description="Chiropractic treatment for whiplash injuries at Frey Clinic of Chiropractic in Napoleon, OH." schemaType="MedicalCondition">
<p>Whiplash occurs when the head is suddenly forced forward and then snapped backward — most commonly during car accidents, but also during sports or falls. Even at low speeds, this rapid motion can damage the muscles, ligaments, and vertebrae of the neck.</p>
<hr class="rule rule--accent" style="margin-block:var(--sp-6);" />
<h2>Symptoms of whiplash</h2>
<p>Whiplash symptoms may not appear immediately — they can develop hours or even days after the injury. Common symptoms include neck pain and stiffness, headaches, dizziness, shoulder pain, and reduced range of motion. Left untreated, whiplash can lead to chronic pain and long-term problems.</p>
<h2>Why chiropractic care matters after whiplash</h2>
<p>Early chiropractic evaluation after a whiplash injury is important. Our chiropractors can identify misalignments and soft tissue damage that may not be visible on standard imaging. Through gentle adjustments and therapeutic support, we help restore proper alignment and promote natural healing.</p>
